"The magnetic bottle's field is the exact Biot–Savart field of two thin rings (complete elliptic integrals), and the proton is stepped with the Boris method, at most {#} rad of gyration per step, which keeps the speed exact. The loss cone and the mirror prediction are the adiabatic (constant μ) theory for the start point's field line; the trajectory itself makes no such assumption, so near the loss cone and at low B₀ the two differ.",
